## Local development

### Todo app

```bash
cd todo-app
npm install
npm run dev
```

### V2 BAGEL WORLD client

```bash
cd client
npm install
npm run dev
```

### V2 BAGEL WORLD server

```bash
cd server
npm install
npm run dev
```

The client expects the V2 API running at `http://localhost:3001` by default.

## Server browser features in the current V2 build

- Create your own server with:
  - server name
  - description
  - password for private servers
  - player limit
  - public/private setting
- View live list of servers
- Search/filter by name and status
- Join public servers directly
- Join private servers with password
- Generate server invite codes
- Owner/admin status scaffold for future moderation controls

## Security and production notes

- Production must use HTTPS and WSS
- Server-side validation is required for all player and economy actions
- All critical state should be persisted in PostgreSQL, not client memory
- Authentication, permissions, moderation and economy validation must be enforced on the server

